\caption(Mask A on the left has four allowed spatial cells; B on the right has five. White means allowed, black means blocked, and gray separates the cells and panels. Both exclude the entire future bottom row and middle-right cell.)
\alttext(Two3x3 masks: top rows are white, bottom rows black. The middle row is white-black-black for A and white-white-black for B.)

> Derive the teacher-forced loss and its partial

Stable Bernoulli negative log likelihood is

$$ \ell_j=\operatorname{softplus}(z_j)-x_jz_j,\qquad
L=\frac1{N64}\sum_{b,j}\ell_{b,j},\qquad
\frac{\partial L}{\partial z_{b,j}}=\frac{\sigma(z_{b,j})-x_{b,j}}{N64}. $$
\alttext(The stable loss is softplus of the logit minus target times logit. Its mean-logit derivative is predicted probability minus target, divided by the total pixel count.)

At z=0, p=.5 and either binary target costs log(2) nats, or one bit. For a
single image, the per-image NLL sums64 terms; the scalar training loss averages
all pixels and rows. Divide nats by log(2) to obtain bits per **binary8x8
pixel**. These are not bits per original28x28 gray pixel. A sigmoid alone
cannot ensure causality: the masked feature paths must exclude the target.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pc_loss_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto t=n::DType::Float64;
 auto z=n::reshape(n::arange(-4,5,1,t),{1,1,9,1}).requires_grad_();
 auto zero=n::models::BernoulliPixels(z,n::zeros(z.shape(),t));
 auto one=n::models::BernoulliPixels(z,n::ones(z.shape(),t));
 auto partial=n::grad(one.loss,{z})[0];
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
 plot.lines(z.to_vector<double>(),zero.pixel_nll.to_vector<double>(),"Target zero",{37,99,235})
  .lines(z.to_vector<double>(),one.pixel_nll.to_vector<double>(),"Target one",{220,38,38})
  .y_limits(-.1,4.9).x_label("Supplied Bernoulli logit").y_label("Nats per pixel")
  .title("Confident wrong logits have a large density cost").save_svg("build/pc_loss_toy.svg");
 std::print("At z=0: target-one NLL={}; mean-loss partial={} (nine pixels).\n",one.pixel_nll.to_vector<double>()[4],partial.to_vector<double>()[4]);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
At z=0: target-one NLL=0.6931471805599453; mean-loss partial=-0.05555555555555555 (nine pixels).
\image(figures/pc_loss_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(At zero logit both losses are log(2). The executed nine-pixel target-one mean has central derivative−.5/9. Stable softplus avoids computing log of a rounded zero probability.)
\alttext(Target-zero negative log likelihood rises with the logit; target-one loss falls. They meet at zero logit with value about.693.)

> Inspect the executed native network

The public API returns the actual preactivation, four ReLU maps and logits.
The diagram traces those boundaries from a real execution; it is not a separate
architectural sketch. Widths remain8 throughout the hidden stack. Four3x3
layers give a nominal9x9 field, with boundary padding and the ordinary masked
CNN blind spot: some earlier pixels remain unreachable through this stack.
The later Jacobian explicitly checks one such dependency, input28 for logit34.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pc_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(8401);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){
  auto o=n::models::PixelCnn(p,x);
  n::model_stage("3x3 A1 to8 + ReLU",x,o.head);
  n::model_stage("3x3 B8 to8 + ReLU",o.head,o.hidden0);
  n::model_stage("3x3 B8 to8 + ReLU",o.hidden0,o.hidden1);
  n::model_stage("3x3 B8 to8 + ReLU",o.hidden1,o.hidden);
  return n::model_stage("1x1 Bernoulli logits",o.hidden,o.logits);
 },"Compact causal PixelCNN:1841 stored values");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
 options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=4;
 auto fig=model.plot(n::zeros({1,8,8,1}),options);
 if(fig.parameter_count()!=1841 || p.size()!=10)throw std::runtime_error("Parameter census");
 fig.save_svg("build/pc_network.svg");
}
```
