> Inspect the actual binary inputs and the fixed learning history

The top row below contains the first eight fit-pool resized gray images; the
bottom row contains their exact deterministic thresholds. The stored data archive
also retains all original28x28 images, digit labels and source IDs. The fixed
small run improves validation likelihood across its three epochs, while its
held-out density still loses to the independent baseline. Replacing the source
protocol with more epochs would answer a different experimental question.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pc_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> a;
 for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/pixel_cnn/data.npz"))a.emplace(key,value);
 auto rows=std::vector<std::int64_t>{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7};
 auto grid=n::concat({n::take_rows(a.at("fit_gray"),rows),n::take_rows(a.at("fit_images"),rows)},0);
 n::save_image_grid(grid,"build/pc_data.png",8,0,1,1,.5,8);
}
