```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pc_history.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> a;
 for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/pixel_cnn/summary.npz"))a.emplace(key,value);
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
 auto baseline=a.at("baseline_bits").item(),test=a.at("test_bits").item();
 plot.lines({1,2,3},a.at("validation_bits").to_vector<double>(),"Validation",{37,99,235})
 .lines({1,3},{baseline,baseline},"Fit-only baseline",{22,163,74})
 .points({3},{test},"Fixed-final test",{220,38,38},6)
 .y_limits(.32,.91).x_label("Fixed epoch").y_label("Bits per binary8x8 pixel")
 .title("Three epochs improve validation; the baseline still wins").save_svg("build/pc_history.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/pc_history.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Validation falls from about.7964 to.5991 bits per binary pixel. The fixed epoch3 test score is.6165; the fit-only independent Bernoulli baseline is.3844. Lower density loss is better.)
\alttext(Blue validation loss falls over epochs1,2,3. The red final-test point remains above the green independent Bernoulli baseline.)

> Check every causal derivative and the remaining blind spot

For every logit j, the program differentiates it with respect to all64 input
pixels. Every entry k>=j is exactly zero. A separate finite-change guard flips
all current/future bits simultaneously and requires every prefix conditional
through j to remain bit identical. The latter catches information leakage that
a local derivative could miss through an inactive ReLU. A single image also
matches its output inside the200-row test batch.

The figure shows the full64x64 absolute Jacobian. Black upper-triangular entries
are structurally forbidden. Earlier-site zeros may also arise from padding,
limited receptive fields, ReLU gates or the standard masked-convolution blind
spot. In particular input28 cannot affect logit34 in this architecture even
though28<34. Strict causality alone does not mean all past information is used.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pc_causality.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::Tensor j;
 for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/pixel_cnn/causality.npz"))if(key=="jacobian")j=n::abs(value);
 auto scaled=n::log1p(100*j);scaled=scaled/n::max(scaled);
 n::save_image_grid(n::reshape(scaled,{1,64,64,1}),"build/pc_causality.png",1,0,1,0,0,6);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/pc_causality.png)
// result_end
\caption(Rows are output logits0..63; columns are input sites0..63. Brightness is log(1+100|derivative|), scaled by the maximum for display. The entire current/future triangle is exactly zero in the saved unscaled Jacobian.)
\alttext(A64x64 derivative matrix has nonzero bands only below the main diagonal. The diagonal and upper-right triangle are black.)

> Generate from zero and complete a preserved prefix

Every unconditional draw begins from an all-zero canvas. Seed8423 produces32
samples; the three epoch snapshots each reuse that seed with16 rows, separating
changes in the fitted density from changes in the random bank. Seed8443 produces
eight completions. The observed first32 raster sites are copied exactly; the
last32 are sampled autoregressively. The completion truth is shown for comparison
and is never supplied after the prefix.

